# Published archive keeps only lib/, example/, doc/, skills/, README.md,
# CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, and pubspec.yaml. Everything below is dev/CI/test
# tooling that must not ship to pub.dev.
#
# EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN IS ROOT-ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, deliberately.
# .pubignore uses gitignore semantics, where a bare `config/` matches a directory
# named `config` at ANY DEPTH -- including `lib/src/config/`. That is not a
# hypothetical: diene_auth_engine 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 both omitted
# `lib/src/config/auth_engine_config.dart` while their public barrel exported it,
# leaving both published archives structurally unusable.
#
# The same hazard applies to every root-only directory below. Anchoring makes the
# exclusions mean what they were written to mean. The publish archive itself is
# the truth: probes/publish-archive-contents.ts runs a real dry-run and sabotages
# this file to prove the shipped usage skill stays included, while
# scripts/validate/dart-package.sh asserts the required source artifacts exist.
/.claude/
/.dart_tool/
/.direnv/
/.github/
/.kagent/
/.kloop/
/config/
/coverage/
/docs/
/nix/
/scripts/
/tasks/
/test/
/tool/
.coderabbit.yaml
.envrc
.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
.markdownlint.json
.prettierrc.yaml
atomi_release.yaml
codecov.yml
flake.lock
flake.nix
Taskfile.yaml
CLAUDE.md
VERSION
